// Introspect — handle-based read-only/write-through reflection for
// `as Introspect` types. `FieldValue` is a small type-erased leaf value;
// anything that isn't one of the kinds below falls back to `Other` (its
// `{:?}` Debug rendering) — this is a fundamental boundary, not a gap: a
// field/method whose type doesn't fit one of these typed variants can
// still be *read* (via `Other`'s Debug fallback) but can never be
// *round-tripped* back into a concrete Rust value, so a method with a
// non-primitive parameter still appears in `introspect()`'s `methods`
// list, but with `isCallable: false` (see emit_struct.rs's
// `introspect_method_is_callable`) — `request`/`modify`/`call` throw a clear
// error rather than being generated a call body that could never work.
//
// `Nested`/`Actor`/`Guard` hold a real, recursively-introspectable
// `Box<dyn Introspect>` for an `'inline`/`'owned`/`'shared` (`Nested`) or
// `'actor`/`'guard` (`Actor`/`Guard` — separate tags, same payload shape,
// for provenance only) field whose OWN type also declares `as Introspect` —
// see `introspect_nested_field_value_expr` (emit_struct.rs) for the exact
// qualifying rules, and the blanket `Introspect` impls just below for how
// `Rc`/`Arc`/`RefCell`/`Mutex`/`RwLock`(+tokio) wrapper layers delegate.
// `Actor`/`Guard` delegate `introspect()` (see those impls) but NOT
// `__introspectAsAny`/`Mut` — a `Field`/`Method` resolved from a nested
// `Actor`/`Guard` value's own `.introspect()` and then used again against
// that same value fails cleanly (the ordinary "wrong instance type" path,
// not a panic) rather than working, a deliberate, documented limitation —
// see docs/book.md's Introspect section.
